==Trivia==
*The Witch is shown to make the practice of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Necromancy necromancy]. Necromancy is a form of magic involving communication with the deceased; either by summoning their spirit as an apparition or raising them bodily.
**In the Japanese language setting of the game, the Witch's name translates to "Necromancer".
*The Witch is 1 of 19 [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] which first existed in Clash of Clans, the others being [[Minions]], [[Archers]], [[Goblins]], [[Skeletons]], [[Barbarians]], [[Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Wizard]], [[Hog Rider]], [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], [[Balloon]], [[Golem]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Phoenix]], [[Lava Hound]], and the [[Archer Queen]].
**The Witch resembles the Level 1-2 Witch from Clash of Clans. Her [[Star Points|Star Level 2 skin]] resembles the Level 3 Witch in Clash of Clans.
**The Witch in Clash Royale shares the same Skeleton spawn sound effect with her Clash of Clans counterpart's.
**In Clash of Clans, the Witch gets around by floating, whereas she walks in Clash Royale.
**Unlike in Clash of Clans, the stats of the Skeletons increase when the Witch is upgraded. In addition, the Witch in Clash Royale does not stop moving when she is spawning Skeletons.
*The Witch is 1 of 15 [[cards]] associated with Skeletons, with the others being [[Bomber]], [[Skeleton Dragons]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Tombstone]], [[Bomb Tower]], [[Guards]], [[Skeleton Army]], Balloon, [[Giant Skeleton]], Wall Breakers, [[Super Witch]], [[Graveyard]], [[Skeleton King]], and of course, Skeletons.
**Despite other cards that spawn Skeletons having 3 [[Star Points|Star Levels]], the Witch only has 2 Star Levels. This trait is also shared with the Tombstone.
*The Witch is one of the first troop cards to be featured in a [[Training Camp|Trainer]]'s [[Battle Decks|deck]], alongside the Minions, Archers, [[Knight]], [[Spear Goblins]], Goblins, Bomber, Skeletons, Barbarians, [[Minion Horde]], [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], [[Musketeer]], Giant, Valkyrie, Wizard, Hog Rider, [[Baby Dragon]], Skeleton Army, P.E.K.K.A, [[Prince]], and Balloon.
*The Witch is one of the first troop cards to receive a card render, alongside the Archers, Knight, Goblins, Bomber, Skeletons, Barbarians, [[Bats]], [[Royal Recruits]], Skeleton Barrel, [[Rascals]], Musketeer, Giant, Valkyrie, Wizard, [[Flying Machine]], Hog Rider, [[Royal Hogs]], [[Dart Goblin]], [[Zappies]], [[Elixir Golem]], Baby Dragon, Skeleton Army, P.E.K.K.A, Prince, Balloon, Giant Skeleton, [[Goblin Giant]], [[Hunter]], [[Electro Dragon]], Wall Breakers, Bowler, Cannon Cart, [[Mega Knight]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Miner]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Ice Wizard]], [[Magic Archer]], [[Bandit]], Lava Hound, [[Night Witch]], and [[Fisherman]].
*The Witch is one of the first cards to ever receive balance changes since [[Version History#The First Update (11/1/2016)|The First Update]], the others being the [[Mortar]], Prince, and [[Goblin Barrel]].
*The Witch is 1 of 3 troops that has been featured with a [[Buff#Stun Attack|Stun Attack]] [[buff]], the others being Spear Goblins and [[Executioner]].
*The Witch is confirmed to be Night Witch's sister, according to the [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p0KUcGDRJjc&t=46s Night Witch Karaoke Contest video] and the Night Witch's description in Clash of Clans.
*According to a Clash of Clans [https://youtube.com/shorts/GmKY_dWMUlk?si=hc2oOztwbFxVPr6C video] on Youtube, the names of the Witch's Skeletons are "Larry", "Kevin", "Toby", and "Carl".
*In [[Arenas|Spooky Town]], a Witch statue can be seen behind the enemy's [[King's Tower]].
*It is rumored that the Super Witch has been summoned from all the other 3 Witches, as demonstrated in the [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VQf90EQVeX8 Super Witch trailer], hence explaining the combination of all the other Witches' abilities.
*The Witch has received the most balance changes of any card in game, having received a total of 46 individual changes.
*When placed right in front of the river, 1 of the Witch's Skeletons will spawn across the river.
*The Witch is featured in non-Clash games. More specifically:
**The Witch, along with the Goblins, Barbarians, Giant, Valkyrie, Wizard, Hog Rider, P.E.K.K.A, and the Archer Queen, were featured as a non-playable opponent in [https://www.chess.com/ Chess].
**The Witch, along with the Archers, Goblins, Barbarians, Musketeer, Wizard, Hog Rider, [[Battle Healer]], Miner, Ice Wizard, and Bandit, are featured as a [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squaddies Squaddie] in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
***Along with the Goblin, Barbarian, Wizard, and Hog Rider, she has the same rarity in both games.
*The Witch, along with the Archers, Goblins, Barbarians, [[Ice Spirit]], Mini P.E.K.K.A, Musketeer, Giant, Wizard, Hog Rider, Prince, and Night Witch, is featured as a sticker in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IMessage iMessage], in a sticker pack called [https://apps.apple.com/us/app/clash-theater-stickers/id1353823484 Clash Theater]. Also, along with the Archers, Goblins, Skeletons, Barbarians, Mini P.E.K.K.A, Musketeer, Wizard, Prince, and [[Princess]], she is also featured in the [https://apps.apple.com/us/app/clash-a-rama/id1182384664 Clash-A-Rama] sticker pack.
*In [[2v2|2v2 Battles]], a Witch placed directly behind the [[King's Tower]] on either side will have one of her Skeletons become stuck behind the King's Tower, unable to move forward unless an opposing troop is very close to it.
*The Witch is the subject of certain cosmetics in the game. More specifically:
**The Witch is the subject of 4 [[Emotes]].
**The Witch is the subject of a few [[Battle Banners|Battle Banner]] items.
***The Swift Summon decoration is created by [https://x.com/suzyq53936155 SuzyQ].
*The initial balance change for Witch on the [[Version History#Balance%20Changes%20(7/6/2022)|End of November 2019 Update]] was an attack time interval decrease to 1 second (from 1.7 seconds), but it was raised to 1.1 seconds [https://x.com/RoyaleAPI_News/status/1197515213089726464?s=20 last minute].
*Before the Witch's card release, the Witch's damage was increased by 9%, and her Skeletons' hitpoints and damage were increased by 8%.

